  "code": "1106",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"127\" data-end=\"253\">The <strong data-start=\"131\" data-end=\"169\">Galactose Quantitative Plasma test</strong> measures the concentration of <strong data-start=\"200\" data-end=\"213\">galactose</strong> in the blood. It is primarily used for:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"255\" data-end=\"588\">\n<li data-start=\"255\" data-end=\"440\">\n<p data-start=\"257\" data-end=\"440\"><strong data-start=\"257\" data-end=\"298\">Screening and diagnosing galactosemia</strong>, a rare inherited metabolic disorder caused by a deficiency of enzymes needed to metabolize galactose (like <strong data-start=\"407\" data-end=\"415\">GALT</strong>, <strong data-start=\"417\" data-end=\"425\">GALK</strong>, or <strong data-start=\"430\" data-end=\"438\">GALE</strong>).</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"441\" data-end=\"521\">\n<p data-start=\"443\" data-end=\"521\">Monitoring infants with known or suspected <strong data-start=\"486\" data-end=\"520\">galactose metabolism disorders</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"522\" data-end=\"588\">\n<p data-start=\"524\" data-end=\"588\">Evaluating unexplained liver dysfunction or failure in newborns.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Elevated Plasma Galactose</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Possible Indications</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Neonatal galactosemia</strong></td>\n<td>Typically due to <strong>GALT deficiency</strong> (classic galactosemia). Accumulated galactose can lead to <strong>jaundice, vomiting, hepatomegaly, and cataracts</strong>.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>GALK or GALE deficiency</strong></td>\n<td>Partial or variant forms of galactosemia with variable symptoms.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Liver dysfunction</strong></td>\n<td>Impaired hepatic clearance of galactose can cause transient elevations. Seen in conditions like <strong>hepatitis</strong> or <strong>biliary atresia</strong> in infants.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Excessive dietary intake</strong></td>\n<td>In rare cases, may reflect high intake of lactose/galactose, especially in neonates with immature liver function.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
